// The REPL end of the same relay: a node driven from somewhere else.
//
// Nothing here is specific to having a serial port -- `repl` names the
// INTERPRETER, so this is what a board with no UART at all would run. Swap the
// two udp buffers for `can` and it is the same six rules.

#buffer Out:4 in  repl                 // what the interpreter printed
#buffer In:4  out repl                 // fed to it, as if typed
#buffer Rx:4  in  udp 55801            // from the console
#buffer Tx:4  out udp 55800 127.0.0.1  // back to it

// Bytes in, straight to the interpreter.
In.dlc = Rx.dlc ? Rx.rx
In = Rx          ? Rx.rx
In.tx = 1        ? Rx.rx

// And everything it prints, back.
Tx.dlc = Out.dlc ? Out.rx
Tx = Out         ? Out.rx
Tx.tx = 1        ? Out.rx
